# Portal UI Design Rules

The portal should look professional, clean, modern, and easy to use.

Design style:
- Use clean spacing.
- Use consistent font sizes.
- Use soft rounded corners.
- Use calm professional colors.
- Use clear active states in sidebar/navigation.
- Avoid clutter.
- Keep pages easy for non-technical users.

Sidebar rules:
- Keep labels short and clear.
- Use consistent icons.
- Use hover states.
- Use visible active states.
- Group related items together.
- Avoid too many nested levels.

Content page rules:
- Use card-based layouts where helpful.
- Use clear headings.
- Use short descriptions.
- Make links easy to scan.
- Keep policy, benefit, form, and portal link sections organized.

Responsive rules:
- Portal must work on desktop, tablet, and mobile.
- Sidebar should collapse or stack nicely on small screens.
- Buttons should be easy to click.
- Text should remain readable.

Keep the design business-friendly, not too playful.
